<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani stock market capitalisation falls.</title>
<headline>Pakistani stock market capitalisation falls.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange said on Tuesday the market capitalisation of listed firms had fallen to 467.652 billion rupees in April from 499.455 billion in March.</p>
<p>						April	March</p>
<p> Listed capital (bln rupees)	   204.458    204.126</p>
<p> Market capitalisation (bln rupees)  467.652    499.455</p>
<p> Turnover of shares (million)	  931.362    936.593</p>
<p> KSE 100 index (points)		 1,538.82   1,574.70</p>
<p> KSE all-share index (points)	   943.73   1,014.79</p>
<p>($1 = 40.43 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
